# Repository layer

Persistence stays in `template.repository`.

- `*Entity`: `@Entity`, `@Table`, sequence id (`GenerationType.SEQUENCE`, `allocationSize = 1`). Lombok data class. No domain logic.
- `*JpaRepository`: `JpaRepository` interface for derived CRUD.
- `*Repository`: `@Repository` facade. Simple CRUD delegates to the JPA interface. Native SQL goes through `EntityManager`.
- `Queries`: `@UtilityClass` of SQL string constants. Do not inline SQL in repository methods.

Mutating repository methods use Spring `@Transactional`. H2 lock and sequence SQL is for dev and tests. Keep it in `Queries`, and note it when the statement is not portable.

Seed data belongs in `data.sql`, `data-dev.sql` (profile `dev`), or `src/test/resources/data-test.sql` (profile `test`). Do not insert rows from Java.

```java
public Optional<ItemEntity> findById(Long id) {
    return jpaRepository.findById(id);
}
```
